Figure 2, the phrase 'qualitatively consistency with perception' should be 'qualitatively consistent with perception'. Additionally, the text refers to 'Table 2' regarding robustness checks for the VGG-19 model, but this table is not included in the provided text, which creates a gap in the information available to the reader. The reference to 'Section 7.3' for experimental details is also not present in the provided text, which may hinder reproducibility for readers relying solely on this document.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008","SRC-016","SRC-020"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Key metrics such as the L1 distance (Equation 2), mutual information (Equation 3), and the contrast sensitivity metric (Equation 4, implied in the text) are clearly introduced with their variables explained. The use of standard symbols for entropy (H), random variables (A_i, C), and image inputs (I, X) is appropriate and consistent throughout the paper. The derivations and explanations of how these metrics are calculated (e.g., averaging over noise levels and neurons) are clear and provide sufficient detail for an expert reader to understand the methodology. There are no significant inconsistencies in the mathematical presentation.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The Markdown table (Table 1) is readable and clearly presents the prediction accuracy metrics (R2, SROCC, RMSE) for different models. The caption text for Figure 1 is detailed, explaining the sub-figures (a, b, c) and the specific DNN model and image scale used. The caption for Figure 2 also provides a clear description of the stimuli and the metric used. However, the paper references several figures (Figures 4-9) and a table (Table 2) that are not included in the provided text. While the captions for the missing figures are not present, the main text references them in a way that suggests they contain important visual evidence (e.g., 'see Figures 4-6' for actual images used). The absence of these visual elements in the text-only format limits the ability to assess their clarity or contribution to understanding, but the textual references are consistent with the described experiments.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"ad6e71579e22bf25c6acb06d6c0049c2156d29da31149ce711472a786d3c6722","paper_id":"BJbD_Pqlg","paper_ordinal":33,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"eb7c23579e534763c8b222c92587bcf86d71f6d189ce07ed955bfebd6e79c3ad","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJbD_Pqlg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"dedc5f6ebae9e13376efd16024e52cd13fa215d0dae7b7483b48d1beb927e8d0","request_identity_sha256":"b53764fb0d3586ba3089189068f267ff86dd5b5f2d98c730a2cb1d58194adac6","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":857,"prompt_tokens":19075,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19932},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"b53764fb0d3586ba3089189068f267ff86dd5b5f2d98c730a2cb1d58194adac6","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}